WEBVTT

00:17:59.353 --> 00:18:01.551
your labor is the contribution
to the miracle.

00:18:01.575 --> 00:18:04.689
And if I'm sitting around waiting
for the miracle to do all of it,

00:18:04.713 --> 00:18:07.715
I'm going to be sitting around waiting
for an awfully long time.

00:18:07.739 --> 00:18:10.798
When people say, "You're so lucky
that you got this inspiration,"

00:18:10.822 --> 00:18:14.280
I think, "Then why am I so tired?
I've been working really, really hard."

00:18:14.304 --> 00:18:18.027
But I also have this subtle sensitivity
to know the difference when I'm working

00:18:18.051 --> 00:18:22.994
between laboring like a mule
and riding on a jet stream.

00:18:23.018 --> 00:18:24.258
And every once in a while,

00:18:24.282 --> 00:18:27.619
once you've been laboring like a mule
for months and months and months,

00:18:27.643 --> 00:18:31.607
suddenly, something really weirdly cosmic
happens, and there's an opening,